Subject: [PATCH 34/37] ice40: an SRAM load over any SPI slave interface
 (TN-02001 Appendix A)

The iCE40 SRAM load took an FtdiSpi only, with CRESET and CDONE on the
FTDI's GPIO bank. Ice40SpiSlaveInterface gives the lines a slave
configuration needs (SPI_SS, SPI_SCK and SPI_SI out, CRESET_B out, CDONE
in, and taking/giving back the bus), and a second Ice40 constructor loads
the SRAM over it. The FTDI path is unchanged: same constructor, same
program_cram(), same commands.

The procedure is TN-02001 (3.1) section 13.2 and Appendix A Table A.1,
timings from DS-02008 (1.5) Table 4.24, and every step is checked:

- CDONE must be high first (a configured iCE40), then fall with CRESET_B
  held low for at least tCRESET_B (200 ns): otherwise no iCE40 is held on
  that reset and no bus line is driven. If CDONE cannot be read there,
  CRESET_B is let go and the error says so.
- SPI_SS low, CRESET_B let go (the iCE40 enters SPI peripheral mode),
  tCR_SCK (1200 us) waited; step 2: SPI_SS high, 8 dummy clocks, SPI_SS
  low.
- The image, msb first, 4 KiB at a time. Each chunk's own SPI_SCK rate,
  and the mean over the image, must be inside the Slave SPI write range
  of 1 to 25 MHz, or the load stops: TN 13.2, once the sync word is sent
  the clock "must be within the range specified in the data sheet", and
  Table A.1 step 4, "Continuous clock is required", so a stall stops it
  as well as a slow cable.
- 100 clocks, CDONE must be high, 49 more (tDONE_IO), SPI_SS high, the
  bus given back.

On any failure the bus is given back first, CRESET_B is let go only if
that worked, an iCE40 already in slave mode is reset to boot from its
flash again, and the error says which of these happened.

SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP are handled for the duration of the load
(the previous handlers are put back after it): the interface's write()
and clocks() stop at the next bit, and the load takes the failure path,
so a load stopped part way leaves the iCE40 booted from its flash rather
than unconfigured. A second signal does not stop that recovery. The
waits are EINTR-safe. SIGKILL cannot be caught.

Flash access on this path is refused: SRAM only.

